From ab244e4973c6302bc3f942d28247fbd57cea7ba5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lewis Purvis <lewisp@imd-tec.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Mar 2026 11:08:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/6] Add support for using the ARM Mali ISP with the AR1335
 sensor with new Device tree overlays for CSI2, CSI3 and dual ISP
 configurations.

* Fixed a bug where the crop window was being set to 0,0,0,0 when the image converter is enabled
* Added RAW10 size information to the format table when the image converter is used
* Added missing image converter interrupts to the Device tree which was causing the IVC and CRU to not come up for CRU0,1,2,3
* The CRU  frame done IRQ  handler when using the image converter doesn't seem to work correctly so the changes have been reverted
* A new translation layer for the ACAMERA V4L2 bridge has been added to allow the Mali ISP firmware to communicate with the V4L2 framework
* New Device tree overlays have been added for the IMDT V2 Plus SBC to support the AR1335 on CSI2 with ISP, CSI3 with ISP and dual ISP configurations
* Fixed a bug with missing interrupts in the RZV2H ISP Device tree which was causing the ISP not to come up correctly
* Updated the defconfig fragment isp.cfg to enable the Mali ISP and related drivers
